---
import SiteLayout from '../layouts/SiteLayout.astro';
---

<SiteLayout current="harness-examples" title="ADK harness examples">
  <section class="section page-section">
    <div class="section-head">
      <p class="eyebrow">Harness examples</p>
      <h1>Google ADK makes the harness visible.</h1>
      <p>
        ADK separates the runtime pieces clearly: the runner executes turns,
        session services hold state and events, confirmations gate risky tools,
        and eval files make trajectories testable.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="detail-grid">
      <article class="detail-card">
        <span>Runner</span>
        <h3>Execution loop as an object.</h3>
        <p>
          The <code>Runner</code> is the entry point for an invocation. It
          connects an agent to session, memory, artifact, and credential
          services.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="detail-card">
        <span>Confirmations</span>
        <h3>Human gates become part of runtime.</h3>
        <p>
          ADK can pause a tool call and request confirmation before executing
          high-impact actions like refunds, work orders, or production changes.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="detail-card">
        <span>Evals</span>
        <h3>Tool trajectories become assertions.</h3>
        <p>
          ADK eval files can encode not only the final response, but also the
          expected tool-use path the harness should produce.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>

    <div class="code-grid">
      <figure class="code-card">
        <figcaption>
          <span>adk_runner_session.py</span>
          <a href="https://adk.dev/runtime/event-loop/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ADK event loop</a>
        </figcaption>
        <pre><code>from google.adk.runners import Runner
from google.adk.sessions import InMemorySessionService
from google.genai import types

session_service = InMemorySessionService()

runner = Runner(
    agent=root_agent,
    app_name="maintenance_agent",
    session_service=session_service,
)

await session_service.create_session(
    app_name="maintenance_agent",
    user_id="operator-7",
    session_id="shift-a",
    state=dict(line="press-2", machine_id="M-42"),
)

message = types.Content(
    role="user",
    parts=[types.Part(text="Diagnose alarm E118 on M-42")],
)

async for event in runner.run_async(
    user_id="operator-7",
    session_id="shift-a",
    new_message=message,
):
    if event.is_final_response():
        print(event.content.parts[0].text)</code></pre>
      </figure>

      <figure class="code-card">
        <figcaption>
          <span>adk_control_points.py</span>
          <a href="https://adk.dev/tools-custom/confirmation/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ADK confirmations</a>
        </figcaption>
        <pre><code>from google.adk.agents import Agent
from google.adk.tools import FunctionTool

root_agent = Agent(
    model="gemini-flash-latest",
    name="maintenance_agent",
    instruction=(
        "Diagnose manufacturing issues. "
        "Never create work orders without confirmation."
    ),
    tools=[
        read_alarm_history,
        fetch_sensor_window,
        FunctionTool(create_work_order, require_confirmation=True),
    ],
)</code></pre>
      </figure>

      <figure class="code-card">
        <figcaption>
          <span>adk_eval_case.test.json</span>
          <a href="https://adk.dev/evaluate/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">ADK evals</a>
        </figcaption>
        <pre><code>&#123;
  "eval_set_id": "manufacturing_diagnostics",
  "eval_cases": [
    &#123;
      "eval_id": "alarm_e118_requires_diagnostics",
      "conversation": [
        &#123;
          "user_content": &#123;
            "parts": [&#123; "text": "Machine M-42 has alarm E118." &#125;],
            "role": "user"
          &#125;,
          "final_response": &#123;
            "parts": [&#123; "text": "I checked recent alarms and sensor windows." &#125;],
            "role": "model"
          &#125;,
          "intermediate_data": &#123;
            "tool_uses": [
              &#123; "name": "read_alarm_history" &#125;,
              &#123; "name": "fetch_sensor_window" &#125;
            ],
            "intermediate_responses": []
          &#125;
        &#125;
      ]
    &#125;
  ]
&#125;</code></pre>
      </figure>
    </div>
  </section>
</SiteLayout>
